374:## 7. Completion boundary and handoff
376:**PROVED new paper results.** FTL1 and its explicit polynomial majorant; the radial-tail refinement and its dimension-independent conditional consequence; the actual binary realization of the divergent radial moments; the elementary Gaussian comparison with stated hypotheses; the exact symmetric cyclic P40 reduction and its qualified relation lower bound; the exact sliding-block energy identities; the stable Gram defect bound with negative spectral mass; and the interval-family obstruction to exponents above 1/2. These have complete paper arguments here. They are not claimed kernel checked, independently refereed, or externally novel.
378:**PROVED quoted inputs.** P40's bounded-variable truncation; P54's sharp rotation superquantile bound; round 4's fixed-complexity QD, defect bound, cover lemma and P53 regularity corrections; P31 and P16 for the stated families; and the precisely attributed BSG/Freiman theorems. These are separated from the new results. The qualitative finite-period estimate also has a direct proof here.
